{
  "experiment": "e2-think-time",
  "title": "E2 — think-time sensitivity (W-syn)",
  "description": "Sweep of the mean think time between an agent's calls at the base workload: shorter think times mean more identical requests in flight at once (PIT aggregation). W-syn: every agent makes callsPerAgent calls to fetch_page with an exponential think time between them; a fraction `overlap` of the calls is drawn from a shared catalog by Zipf(alpha), the rest ask for documents no other call asks for. Same seeds at every point; reductions are paired by seed against B0 (and B1). B5 is plain MCP with one shared exact-match cache at the edge keyed by the arguments as sent, as MCP gateways ship it (ADR-036); it is run on the same seeds.",
  "kind": "sweep",
  "seeds": {
    "first": 1,
    "count": 30
  },
  "modes": [
    "B0",
    "B1",
    "B2",
    "B3",
    "B5"
  ],
